Mitcad's patch to OCCT 8.0.1, under OCCT's licence:
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-only WITH OCCT-exception-1.0

Fillets and chamfers: a closed contour of several edges whose blend
consumes a face all round, its contact running along that face's edges.

E.g. a slot (two lines and two half circles) under a counterbore of the
same shape 0.5 wider: the counterbore's floor is a ledge 0.5 wide all round
the slot's rim, and the rim rounded or chamfered with 0.5 consumes it. Each
piece of the closed stripe has its contact along a whole edge of the
ledge (ChFi3d_ContactsAlongFaceEdges, patch 0014), whose ends at the
edge's vertices become those vertices. At the stripe's start and end,
though, the stripe kept the point it had made for its start beside that
vertex, and the topological build failed on the two (TopoDS_Builder::Add
in TopOpeBRepBuild_Builder::MakeEdges); the fillet was built 0.1 % smaller
by Mitcad, leaving a ledge of 0.5 micrometres on which the next rounding
failed. As for a contact along a closed edge, the stripe's point there is
now the vertex, for closed and periodic spines. A round hole (one closed
edge) built before and builds the same.
